{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "וירח", :translit "va-yarach", :gloss "and he smelled"} {:he "וירח ה' את ריח הניחוח", :translit "va-yarach HaShem et rei'ach ha-nicho'ach", :gloss "and the LORD smelled the pleasing fragrance"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וירח" "וירח ה' את ריח הניחוח"]}], :frame {:text "The two occurrences of וירח are linked: the fragrance Isaac smelled (Genesis 27:27) corresponds to the pleasing fragrance the LORD smelled from Noah's offering (Genesis 8:21). The rabbis identify Isaac's fragrance with the fragrance of Garden of Eden. Hosea 14:7 promises that Israel's shoots will blossom and blossom 'like the Lebanon,' which the Talmud interprets as the Temple that atones for Israel.", :sources ["Genesis 8:21" "Hosea 14:7" "Megillah 12b" "Bereshit Rabbah 66:3"]}} {:quotes [{:he "וירח", :translit "va-yarach", :gloss "and he smelled"} {:he "יום פסח", :translit "yom pesach", :gloss "day of Passover"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "וירח", :b "יום פסח"}], :frame {:text "Genesis Rabbah 63:12 records that Isaac said to Jacob, 'The time has come for the sons to be blessed,' referring to the night of Passover when Israel offers the paschal lamb and is blessed. The association of the Exodus narrative with Passover is established throughout Exodus 12.", :sources ["Genesis Rabbah 63:12" "Exodus 12"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ריח", :translit "rei'ach", :gloss "fragrance"} {:he "ליל פסח", :translit "leil pesach", :gloss "night of Passover"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "ריח", :b "ליל פסח"}], :frame {:text "Genesis Rabbah 63:12 records that Isaac told Jacob, 'The time has come for the sons to be blessed,' referring to the night of Passover. The paschal lamb is eaten at night as commanded in Exodus 12:8.", :sources ["Genesis Rabbah 63:12" "Exodus 12:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כריח", :translit "k'rei'ach", :gloss "like the fragrance"} {:he "כריח שדה", :translit "k'rei'ach sadeh", :gloss "like the fragrance of a field"} {:he "כריח שדה לבנון", :translit "k'rei'ach sadeh levanon", :gloss "like the fragrance of the field of Lebanon"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["כריח שדה" "כריח שדה לבנון"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase כריח שדה appears in Genesis 27:27 of Isaac and in Hosea 14:7. Hosea's 'Lebanon' is read as a name for the Temple: the Midrash states 'Lebanon — this is the Sanctuary,' based on the parallel between Lebanon's beauty and the Temple's; the Talmud likewise interprets Hosea 14:7's blossoming 'like the Lebanon' as the Temple. The offering that rises 'from Lebanon' is thus the Temple service.", :sources ["Genesis 27:27" "Hosea 14:7" "Bereshit Rabbah 66:3" "Yoma 12a" "Megillah 12b"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["וירח" "וירח ה' את ריח הניחוח"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "וירח", :refs ["Genesis 8:21" "Genesis 27:27" "Joshua 10:12" "Joshua 10:13" "Isaiah 13:10" "Ezekiel 32:7" "Joel 2:10" "Joel 4:15"], :n 11, :lens :exact} {:phrase "וירח ה' את ריח הניחוח", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]} {:kind :gematria, :a "וירח", :a-value 224, :b "יום פסח", :b-value 204, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "ריח", :a-value 218, :b "ליל פסח", :b-value 218, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["כריח שדה" "כריח שדה לבנון"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "כריח שדה", :refs ["Genesis 27:27"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כריח שדה לבנון", :refs [], :n 0, :lens :plene-insensitive}]}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:08:45.138243962Z", :model "glm-5.2"}